# XCU chmod
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Tests run in the private directory the driver gives. Scaffolding uses only POSIX utilities; setup problems are UNRESOLVED.

assertion  XCU.chmod.001
anchor     utilities/chmod.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/chmod.html#OPERANDS
class      required
says       chmod with an octal mode sets the permission bits absolutely,
           for each file operand.
test       t/001-octal.sh

assertion  XCU.chmod.002
anchor     utilities/chmod.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       chmod with a symbolic mode that names who applies +, - and = to
           the named classes only, several clauses separated by commas.
test       t/002-symbolic-who.sh

assertion  XCU.chmod.003
anchor     utilities/chmod.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       Without who, + - and = affect the classes except the bits set
           in the file creation mask.
test       t/003-symbolic-no-who.sh

assertion  XCU.chmod.004
anchor     utilities/chmod.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       One clause may carry several actions, applied in order.
test       t/004-multiple-actions.sh

assertion  XCU.chmod.005
anchor     utilities/chmod.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       The permission letters u, g and o after an operator copy the
           current permissions of that class.
test       t/005-permcopy.sh

assertion  XCU.chmod.006
anchor     utilities/chmod.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       The permission X sets execute/search only for directories and
           for files that already have an execute bit.
test       t/006-perm-X.sh

assertion  XCU.chmod.007
anchor     utilities/chmod.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       On a regular file with an execute bit, u+s sets and u-s clears
           set-user-ID, octal 4755 sets it and 755 clears it, and o+s
           changes nothing and is not an error.
test       t/007-setuid.sh

assertion  XCU.chmod.008
anchor     utilities/chmod.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       On a directory, a+t or t alone sets the sticky bit, octal 1777
           sets it, and an octal mode without it clears it.
test       t/008-sticky.sh

assertion  XCU.chmod.009
anchor     utilities/chmod.html#OPTIONS
class      required
says       chmod -R changes the mode of a directory operand and of every
           file below it.
test       t/009-option-R.sh

assertion  XCU.chmod.010
anchor     utilities/chmod.html#EXIT STATUS
anchor     utilities/V3_chap01.html#1.4
class      required
says       If one file cannot be changed, chmod diagnoses it, changes the
           others, and exits non-zero.
test       t/010-error-continue.sh
